# Vulnerabilities in the deployer image that are genuinely blocked on an
# upstream fix, not something we can patch ourselves. Any NEW finding not
# listed here still fails the scan.
#
# Google shipped a fix for the go1.26.5 stdlib CVEs on ~2026-09-21 — the
# base image's kubectl (now v1.37) and helm are built with go1.26.6/1.27.1
# respectively, confirmed clean by a full rescan. See
# https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/marketplace-k8s-app-tools/issues/688
# (still open as of this cleanup; comment there tracked it as fixed).

# usr/local/bin/nk (ours, built from source): nkeys v0.4.16 (the latest
# published release) only pulls golang.org/x/crypto v0.52.0; this CVE's
# fix needs 0.55.0, not yet available in any nkeys release. Also present
# in Google's own helm binary as of the last scan that found it.
CVE-2026-56854

# Google's deployer_helm base image (13.0.13, 2026-10-23). Go binaries:
# opt/kubectl/v1.37/kubectl is built with go1.26.8 and old x/net / x/text
# (the latest official kubectl, v1.37.1, is also built with go1.26.8), and
# usr/local/bin/helm with go1.27.2. The Go stdlib fixes need go1.26.9-1.26.10
# / go1.27.2-1.27.3. Our own nk binary is built with go1.26.10 and is not
# affected. Remove these once a rescan of a newer base image comes back clean.
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-97031
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-111943
CVE-2026-56851

# Same base image: Python packages shipped with Google's deployer tooling
# (setuptools 70.3.0, urllib3 2.7.0, msgpack 1.1.2). Not upgraded here to
# avoid changing the dependencies of Google's deployer scripts.
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
